Algorithm:
 Start the program.
 Input equipment names and wiring connections with their weights.
 Sort the edges in ascending order of weight.
 Apply Kruskal's algorithm using Disjoint Set Union.
 Select edges that do not create cycles.
 Display each selected edge, its weight, and the running total cost.
 Check whether V - 1 edges were selected.
 If fewer than V - 1 edges were selected, report that the graph is disconnected.
 Ask the user whether an edge weight should be updated.
 If yes, update the specified connection's weight.
 Apply Kruskal's algorithm again and display the new result.
 Stop.
